# Capturia runs the agent on your own API key. Get a free Gemini key at
# https://aistudio.google.com and paste it here (copy this file to .env.local).
# Heads up for PUBLIC deploys: this server-side key powers /studio for anyone
# who can reach your deployment — use a free-tier key (one on a Google Cloud
# project with NO billing account: it hits a hard quota instead of a bill) and
# turn on the demo limits below so one visitor can't exhaust it.
GOOGLE_GENERATIVE_AI_API_KEY=

# Optional: spend brake for a public demo deploy. Off unless set. Applies to
# requests that could spend the server env key above (BYOK desktop callers use
# their own key and are never limited). Counters live in the Upstash Redis
# below when configured (recommended on serverless), else in-process. Per-IP
# buckets store a salted hash, never the IP, and expire within minutes; the
# global daily bucket holds a bare count for up to two days.
# The DAILY budget is the load-bearing spend cap: the per-IP limit rides on a
# spoofable header, so on its own it is a courtesy throttle, not protection.
# CAPTURIA_DEMO_IP_RPM=6              # per-visitor requests per minute
# CAPTURIA_DEMO_DAILY_REQUESTS=500    # total requests per UTC day, all visitors
# CAPTURIA_DEMO_SALT=                 # IP-hash salt; the default is a public
#                                     # constant, so set a random string here
#                                     # for stronger unlinkability

# Optional: other providers. Deck codegen and the agent can run on Claude or
# OpenAI instead of Gemini.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# OPENAI_API_KEY=

# Optional: pick the server-side model. CAPTURIA_PROVIDER chooses a provider
# default (gemini | claude | openai); CAPTURIA_MODEL pins an exact ai-sdk spec
# and wins over CAPTURIA_PROVIDER (see lib/server-keys.ts).
# CAPTURIA_PROVIDER=gemini
# CAPTURIA_MODEL=google/gemini-2.5-flash-lite

# Optional: the public origin audience phones use for vote rooms and the QR
# code. For LAN voting with `next dev`, set your LAN address; for a deployed
# studio, your public URL. Also baked into desktop builds by build:electron
# (unset = the packaged app ships QR-less and shows an in-app notice).
# NEXT_PUBLIC_CAPTURIA_ORIGIN=http://192.168.1.20:3000

# Optional: audience-vote store for SERVERLESS self-hosts only. The default
# in-memory room store is all a local dev server or a long-lived self-host
# needs. On a serverless deploy, bring your own Redis over the Upstash REST
# protocol (the free tier works), then certify the deploy with:
#   CAPTURIA_BASE_URL=https://your-deploy node scripts/verify-vote-redis.mjs
# UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_URL=
# UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_TOKEN=
